    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d550">

                <pb facs="0685" n="571" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg571"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/425: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-01-24T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                                1924—8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>25. With reference to your telegram 5 of January 4, Schwerin<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d550-f1"/> informs Department that he would be very glad if a
                    solution could be found which would end the continued agitation to which the
                    Chinese are subjected because of the Federal contract. He does not believe,
                    however, that the Federal Telegraph Company can take over the Mitsui station at
                    Peking to relieve the Japanese of a bad bargain. He says that should his company
                    try to unite with the Japanese, the latter would insist upon sharing in the
                    activities of all the company’s stations. He also says that this would nullify
                    all the efforts of his company to give the American and Chinese people the right
                    of communication with each other without interference from any other
                    country.</p>
                <p>Schwerin says he cannot go back to China before March.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d550-f1" n="6" xml:id="d550-f1-content">
                <p>R. P. Schwerin, president of the Federal Telegraph Co. of Delaware.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
